const e="cante-de-las-minas-flamenco-festival",l=2026,t="Read from the festival bases page and the full texts of the four bases PDFs (Cante 13 pages, Guitarra 11, Baile 12, Instrumentista 11) and the registration form page. Placed: contest dates, eligibility per contest, registration steps and online form fields, documents per contest, phases (selection, selective tests, semifinals, final), accompanists, prizes (amounts, trophies, payment steps), the Special Jury Prize, the Mariano Conde and Festivales Region de Murcia prizes, expenses paid to contestants, promotion recital duties of winners, recording rights, conduct and penalties, no-claim rule, diplomas, and the Las Minas Flamenco Tour 26/27 conditions. Edition facts are Variables: dates, deadlines, the draw time, addresses, the demo contact, the website, the tour cities and one news item. The bases do NOT print: an entry fee, a minimum age for Instrumentista, a time limit for the Baile final, any mark scheme or points, or a phone number. The web page and the bases print different registration dates: the web page says the period is extended to 20 June 2026 (1 July for Instrumentista) while the bases print 1 June 2026 (1 July for Instrumentista); the extended dates are used. The Guitarra bases place the selective tests between June and July in the bases and May to June in Annex I. The web page prints two copies of the registration notice, the second one calling the festival the 66th edition; the 65th is used. The web page says the dance contest has two forms of expression and a Desplante prize in men's and women's categories; the bases print neither. The template items Cante - Grupo I to III hold the prize and time rules of the Cante contest; the Lampara Minera, Special Jury Prize and region prize are described once in the Prizes section. Spanish text is translated to plain English; accents are left out because the template names are written without them.",a=JSON.parse(`{"Title":"Rules & Criteria","Subtitle":"Festival Internacional del Cante de las Minas 2026, 65th edition (La Union, Murcia). Read these rules before you register.","NoticeTitle":"Please Read Before Registering","Notice":"The contests are held on {{ContestDates}} in {{FestivalVenue}}. Register by {{RegistrationDeadline}} for Cante, Guitarra and Baile, and by {{InstrumentistaDeadline}} for Instrumentista. Registering means you accept the bases and the jury's decision. The minimum age for Cante, Guitarra and Baile is 16 at the start of the contest.","Notes":["Registration is preferably online on the festival website. If you cannot register online, send the form and documents by post to {{RegistrationAddress}}.","The Instrumentista contest has no selective tests.","The bases are in Spanish. This page gives them in plain English."],"Sections":[{"Key":"general","Title":"General Rules","Items":["The Fundacion Cante de las Minas (Cante de las Minas Foundation) holds the 65th Festival Internacional del Cante de las Minas, from {{FestivalDates}}.","The festival has four contests: the 65th Concurso de Cante Flamenco, the 46th Concurso de Guitarra Flamenca, the 32nd Concurso de Baile Flamenco and the 18th Concurso de Instrumentista Flamenco.","All four contests are held in La Union on {{ContestDates}}.","Registering for a contest means you fully accept its bases and the decision of the jury.","The performances at the festival can be recorded, copied, distributed and shown to the public, in whole or in part, in any format and on radio, television, cable, fibre optic, digital or the internet, worldwide and for the longest time the law allows. This applies even if you win no prize. The rights of other people in the works performed are not affected.","The selective tests, the semifinals and the final are recorded in full for the use of the jury and for promotion of the contests, if the organisation decides so.","When you register, you accept these recording rules."]},{"Key":"eligibility","Title":"Eligibility","Items":["Cante (singing): any singer, professional or not, can take part. The exceptions are anyone who has already won the Lampara Minera and anyone who has not turned 16 when the contest starts.","Guitarra (guitar): any guitarist, professional or not, can take part. The exceptions are anyone who has already won the Bordon Minero and anyone who has not turned 16 when the contest starts.","Baile (dance): any dancer, professional or not, can take part. The exceptions are anyone who has already won the Desplante trophy and anyone who has not turned 16 when the contest starts.","Instrumentista (instrumentalist): any instrumentalist, professional or not, alone or as part of a group, can take part. The exception is anyone who has already won the trophy El Filon. The bases print no minimum age for this contest.","Instrumentista accepts every kind of instrument: melodic or single-voice instruments (violin, flute, saxophone and others), polyphonic instruments (piano, keyboards and others) and percussion (cajon, drums, castanets and others), acoustic or electronic (electric guitar and bass, synthesizers, experimental music, electronic music and others). The flamenco guitar is the one exception: it has its own contest.","Cantaores Jovenes (young singers): a special prize for singers who have not turned 30 when the contest starts, and who won none of the other prizes in this edition or in earlier editions.","Premio de Guitarra Mariano Conde: guitarists who appear during the contest, as soloists or as accompanists, aged 16 to 30 completed on the date of the contest.","Premio Festivales Region de Murcia: artists born in or living in the Region of Murcia who reach the final of any of the four contests.","The bank account for prize payments must be held by the contestant, alone or jointly, and its IBAN must belong to an account of Spanish residence.","A contestant who does not appear at a selective test is out of the contest and cannot enter the next two editions, unless there is a justified reason that the organisation accepts."]},{"Key":"registration","Title":"How to Register","Items":["Registration is preferably digital, with the electronic form on the festival website {{FestivalWebsite}}.","If you cannot register online, download the registration form (boletin de inscripcion) from the website, fill it in and send it by ordinary post, with the required documents in one envelope, to {{RegistrationAddress}}.","The documents you send depend on the contest. They are listed under each competition.","Filling in the form, online or by hand, means you accept all the obligations of registering.","The last date to register for Cante, Guitarra and Baile is {{RegistrationDeadline}}. The last date to register for Instrumentista is {{InstrumentistaDeadline}}.","The online form asks for your first name, surname, artistic name (if you have one), ID number (DNI, NIF or NIE), city and date of birth, city of residence, full address, postal code, landline (optional), mobile number and email (entered twice).","The online form asks which category you enter: Cante, Guitarra, Baile or Instrumentista.","The online form asks whether you need the festival to provide a guitarist, and which palos (flamenco styles) you will perform.","The online form asks whether you took part in the selective tests of any of the 3 previous editions.","For Baile and Instrumentista only, the form asks for the artists who accompany you and your technical requirements.","The form asks for a link to an audiovisual demo. The festival recommends sending videos or audio through services such as WeTransfer, or a link to cloud files such as Dropbox or YouTube, to {{ContestsContact}}.","The form asks for the IBAN of the bank account where you want to be paid.","The form asks for an ID-style photograph, an artistic and professional curriculum, and a certificate from the bank that shows you hold the account.","You must accept the Legal Notice and the Privacy Policy, confirm that you downloaded and read the bases and agree to them, and confirm that you read the conditions of the tour.","When the organisation receives your registration form, it sends you the conditions for taking part in the Las Minas Flamenco Tour.","The bases print no entry fee."]},{"Key":"dates","Title":"Important Dates","Items":["The festival is held from {{FestivalDates}}.","The contests are held on {{ContestDates}}.","Last date to register for Cante, Guitarra and Baile: {{RegistrationDeadline}}. Last date to register for Instrumentista: {{InstrumentistaDeadline}}.","Selective tests (Cante, Guitarra and Baile): {{SelectiveTestsPeriod}}","Semifinals: {{SemifinalDates}}, in La Union.","The semifinal results, with the list of those who go to the final, are made public {{SemifinalResultsTime}}.","Final: {{FinalDate}}, in La Union.","Public draw for the Lampara Minera: {{LamparaDrawTime}}, at {{LamparaDrawVenue}}.","Instrumentista finalists must state the works they will play on {{InstrumentistaFinalWorksTime}}."]},{"Key":"venue","Title":"Venue","Items":["The contests are held in {{FestivalVenue}}.","The semifinals and the final are held in La Union. The selective tests are held in several towns in Spain.","The organisation tries to give each contestant the selective test nearest to their home.","The Foundation office for postal registration is at {{RegistrationAddress}}."]},{"Key":"levels","Title":"Phases of the Contest","Items":["Phase 1, selection: the festival jury chooses, from the registered contestants, those who go to the next phase. The choice is based on the audiovisual demos the contestants send. The list of those chosen is made public.","The jury may be present in person or online, and all members score the performances of the test.","Phase 2, selective tests (pruebas selectivas), for Cante, Guitarra and Baile: public tests held in several towns in Spain, {{SelectiveTestsPeriod}}","The organisation sets the dates and places of the selective tests and gives enough notice. It offers two alternative dates, and the contestant must choose one beforehand.","The call for each contestant is made once only, and the contestant must perform on the date and at the place given.","The official jury of the festival scores the selective tests. For Guitarra and Baile, the jury classifies as many contestants as it thinks fit.","Instrumentista has no selective tests. The jury chooses the semifinalists by watching the video material each contestant sends. The list of semifinalists is made public with the day each one performs.","Phase 3, semifinals: held in La Union on {{SemifinalDates}}. The jury chooses who goes to the final and, for Cante, the cante styles of each contestant in the groups.","The jury may choose nobody for the final. In Guitarra, Baile and Instrumentista the prize is then void.","The jury makes a record (acta) of each test it judges.","The semifinal results, with the list of those chosen for the final, are made public {{SemifinalResultsTime}}.","Phase 4, final: held in La Union on {{FinalDate}}. The organisation sets the order in which the contestants perform.","When the performances end, the jury makes public the record with the prize winners in each contest and group."]},{"Key":"teams","Title":"Accompanists and Groups","Items":["Cante: bring your own guitarist, unless you ask the Foundation for an official festival guitarist in writing, by any means that leaves a record.","The organisation names the official guitarists before the contest starts. You choose which one you want, before your test, when you are called.","Guitarra: during the semifinals and the final, the guitarist can be accompanied by at most two palmeros (hand clappers) and one percussionist. The accompaniment must be declared on the registration form, and the contestant pays for the accompanists.","Baile and Instrumentista: you list on the registration form the members of your group (name, surname and role)."]},{"Key":"conduct","Title":"Conduct and Penalties","Items":["Dedications and any other kind of proclamation during a performance are strictly forbidden. They can lead to disqualification. This applies in the selective tests, the semifinals and the final.","The Foundation can take legal action against contestants who insult or defame, in person or in any written, digital or audiovisual way, or who try to attack, a member of the jury or the festival organisation, because they disagree with the jury's decision.","The penalty for this is a ban from the contest (lifetime in Guitarra, Baile and Instrumentista; lifetime or for a time in Cante) and withdrawal of any prize won."]},{"Key":"judging","Title":"Judging","Items":["The same jury, chosen by the organisation, judges all phases of a contest.","The jury's decision cannot be appealed."]},{"Key":"complaints","Title":"Complaints","Items":["No claim can be made against the jury's decision in the semifinals or in the final."]},{"Key":"prizes","Title":"Prizes","Items":["Lampara Minera (the top prize of the Cante contest and the highest honour of the festival): the trophy of this name and 15,000 euros. This prize includes any first prizes the winner could also have won in other Cante groups.","To win the Lampara Minera, the singer must qualify for the final in the cante por mineras. The singer must also perform, as well as the minera, one cante of the Mining Cantes group (Cartageneras, Tarantas or the other cantes).","If a singer is not chosen for the final in any Mining cante but is chosen in the minera, one mining cante is performed by public draw. The draw is held {{LamparaDrawTime}}, at {{LamparaDrawVenue}}.","To win the Lampara Minera, the singer must also have qualified for the final in a cante of Group II or Group III.","The Lampara Minera goes to the contestant who shows good command and knowledge of mining cantes first of all and, in this edition, also shows skill in other flamenco styles.","The Lampara Minera money is paid as 10,000 euros after the general prize-giving of all contests, and the rest after the fourth of the promotion recitals.","Cante, Group I: Cartageneras, a single prize of 3,000 euros. Tarantas, a single prize of 3,000 euros. Murcianas and other mining cantes (taranto, levantica, fandango minero, cantes de madrugada and others), a single prize of 3,000 euros.","Cante, Group II (cantes of Malaga, Granada, Cordoba and Huelva and other cantes derived from the Andalusian fandango): first prize, a single prize of 3,000 euros.","Cante, Group III A (tonas, siguiriyas, soleares, bulerias por solea, canas, polos, livianas and serranas): a single prize of 2,000 euros.","Cante, Group III B (bulerias, cantinas, tangos, tientos, peteneras, farrucas, personal fandangos and others): a single prize of 2,000 euros.","Cantaores Jovenes: a special prize of 2,000 euros.","Guitarra: first prize of 6,000 euros and, when it applies, the trophy Bordon Minero. A first payment of 4,000 euros is made and the rest after the promotion recitals. Second prize of 2,000 euros and a diploma. The jury can declare any prize void.","Baile: first prize of 6,000 euros and, when it applies, the trophy El Desplante, for the best dancer in the jury's view. A first payment of 4,000 euros is made and the remaining 2,000 euros after the promotion recitals. Second prize of 3,000 euros and a diploma.","Instrumentista: first prize of 6,000 euros and, when it applies, the trophy El Filon. A first payment of 4,000 euros is made and the rest after the promotion recitals. Second prize of 2,000 euros and a diploma.","Premio especial del Jurado (Special Jury Prize): 1,000 euros for the best accompanying artist in the Cante, Baile and Instrumentista contests, as the jury decides.","Premio de Guitarra Mariano Conde: a diploma from the organisation and a Mariano Conde guitar worth 4,000 euros.","Premio Festivales Region de Murcia: a trophy and 1,000 euros. It can be won together with any other big prize. If another prize is won, the money is replaced by the bigger amount.","Prize amounts are paid after the tax withholding that the law on personal income tax sets. All payments are made by bank transfer to the account the contestants give when they register."]},{"Key":"reporting","Title":"After the Contest","Items":["Any contestant who passed the selection and actually performs in the semifinals or the final gets a diploma proving they took part in the festival, if they ask for it (printed in the Cante and Guitarra bases).","Prize winners must give the Foundation the receipts (invoices in the Foundation's name) for the travel and lodging costs the Foundation pays for the promotion recitals. Costs that are not travel or lodging, or have no invoice in the name of the Fundacion Cante de las Minas, are not paid."]},{"Key":"other","Title":"Las Minas Flamenco Tour 2026/27","Items":["The festival plans the second edition of the annual tour LAS MINAS FLAMENCO TOUR in the 2026/27 season (between September 2026 and June 2027), in several cities in Spain.","The tour is made up of the main winners of the La Union festival. SO-LA-NA Entertainment produces and directs it, and is the official producer chosen by the festival.","The cast is preferably the winners or finalists of the 2026 festival. SO-LA-NA chooses the final cast at its own discretion.","Taking part in the tour is the winners' own choice. The fees and daily allowances are fixed in advance and are sent when the registration form is received.","The cities planned for the tour are {{TourCities}}","The final list of cities, dates and theatres is being prepared. The artist is told in time to block the date."]}],"Documents":[{"Title":"Bases de los concursos 2026 (all four contests)","Url":"https://festivalcantedelasminas.org/bases-concursos-2026/"},{"Title":"Bases of the LXV Concurso de Cante Flamenco","Url":"https://festivalcantedelasminas.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/bases_Cante_2026_Cante_de_las_Minas.pdf"},{"Title":"Bases of the XLVI Concurso de Guitarra Flamenca","Url":"https://festivalcantedelasminas.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/bases_Guitarra_2026_Cante_de_las_Minas.pdf"},{"Title":"Bases of the XXXII Concurso de Baile Flamenco","Url":"https://festivalcantedelasminas.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/bases_Baile_2026_Cante_de_las_Minas.pdf"},{"Title":"Bases of the XVIII Concurso de Instrumentista Flamenco","Url":"https://festivalcantedelasminas.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/bases_Instrumentista_2026_Cante_de_las_Minas.pdf"},{"Title":"Registration form (boletin de inscripcion) 2026","Url":"https://festivalcantedelasminas.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Boletin-de-inscripcion-CANTE-MINAS-2026.pdf"},{"Title":"Legal Notice (Aviso Legal)","Url":"https://festivalcantedelasminas.org/avisos-legales"},{"Title":"Privacy Policy (Politica de Privacidad)","Url":"https://festivalcantedelasminas.org/politica-de-privacidad"}]}`),n=[],o=[{AgeGroup:"Open (16+)",Source:"Bases del LXV Concurso de Cante Flamenco 2026, base SEGUNDA; Bases del XLVI Concurso de Guitarra Flamenca 2026, base SEGUNDA; Bases del XXXII Concurso de Baile Flamenco 2026, base SEGUNDA",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Cante, Guitarra and Baile: you must have turned 16 when the contest starts.","Past winners of the top trophy of the contest (Lampara Minera, Bordon Minero or Desplante) cannot take part again."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:["The Instrumentista bases print no minimum age."]},Markdown:`## Rules
- Cante, Guitarra and Baile: you must have turned 16 when the contest starts.
- Past winners of the top trophy of the contest (Lampara Minera, Bordon Minero or Desplante) cannot take part again.

## Notes for participants
- The Instrumentista bases print no minimum age.`},{AgeGroup:"Cant. Jovenes",Source:"Bases del LXV Concurso de Cante Flamenco 2026, base TERCERA, Cantaores Jovenes",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Cantaores Jovenes are singers who have not turned 30 when the contest starts.","The special prize can only go to a contestant who won none of the other prizes of the Cante contest in this edition or in earlier editions."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- Cantaores Jovenes are singers who have not turned 30 when the contest starts.
- The special prize can only go to a contestant who won none of the other prizes of the Cante contest in this edition or in earlier editions.`},{AgeGroup:"Premio Conde",Source:"Bases del LXV Concurso de Cante Flamenco 2026, base CUARTA; Bases del XLVI Concurso de Guitarra Flamenca 2026, base OCTAVA",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["The Premio de Guitarra Mariano Conde can go, at the jury's choice, to guitarists who appear during the contest, as soloists or as accompanists, aged 16 to 30 completed on the date of the contest."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:["The prize is a diploma from the organisation and a Mariano Conde guitar worth 4,000 euros."]},Markdown:`## Rules
- The Premio de Guitarra Mariano Conde can go, at the jury's choice, to guitarists who appear during the contest, as soloists or as accompanists, aged 16 to 30 completed on the date of the contest.

## Notes for participants
- The prize is a diploma from the organisation and a Mariano Conde guitar worth 4,000 euros.`}],s=JSON.parse(`[{"Title":"Cante - Grupo I: Cartageneras","Source":"Bases del LXV Concurso de Cante Flamenco 2026, bases TERCERA to DUODECIMA","Sections":{"About":["Group I, mining cantes: Cartageneras. A single prize.","The contestant sings one letra (verse) only."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Expenses paid to contestants at the selective tests: 30 euros for a local singer (home town less than 60 km from the test) and 150 euros for a non-local singer (more than 60 km).","Expenses paid to contestants who reach the semifinals: 30 euros for a local singer and 150 euros for a non-local singer.","A contestant in the final who wins no prize is paid 600 euros once, which replaces the semifinal expenses. Prize winners get no participation expenses.","The Lampara Minera winner must give at least four promotion recitals: one at the Gala de Premiados of the next festival and the others on dates the organisation decides.","The winners of the other Cante prizes, if they are not the Lampara Minera winner, must give at least one promotion recital on the date, at the place and on the terms the organisation decides.","For the promotion recitals the organisation pays only the travel and lodging of the winner and the accompanying guitarist. No fee is paid.","Documents to send by post: a photograph of the artist, an artistic curriculum, a recent video recording of the cantes you enter with, a bank certificate (or a copy of the savings book) showing you as holder or joint holder with an IBAN of a Spanish account, and a note saying whether you have your own guitarist or want one from the festival.","A contestant can perform at most four cantes, plus the cante of the draw for the Lampara Minera if it applies."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The jury values originality of style and of repertoire, musical and literary, and the singer's own artistic contributions, within the orthodoxy of each cante."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Group I, mining cantes: Cartageneras. A single prize.\\n- The contestant sings one letra (verse) only.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Expenses paid to contestants at the selective tests: 30 euros for a local singer (home town less than 60 km from the test) and 150 euros for a non-local singer (more than 60 km).\\n- Expenses paid to contestants who reach the semifinals: 30 euros for a local singer and 150 euros for a non-local singer.\\n- A contestant in the final who wins no prize is paid 600 euros once, which replaces the semifinal expenses. Prize winners get no participation expenses.\\n- The Lampara Minera winner must give at least four promotion recitals: one at the Gala de Premiados of the next festival and the others on dates the organisation decides.\\n- The winners of the other Cante prizes, if they are not the Lampara Minera winner, must give at least one promotion recital on the date, at the place and on the terms the organisation decides.\\n- For the promotion recitals the organisation pays only the travel and lodging of the winner and the accompanying guitarist. No fee is paid.\\n- Documents to send by post: a photograph of the artist, an artistic curriculum, a recent video recording of the cantes you enter with, a bank certificate (or a copy of the savings book) showing you as holder or joint holder with an IBAN of a Spanish account, and a note saying whether you have your own guitarist or want one from the festival.\\n- A contestant can perform at most four cantes, plus the cante of the draw for the Lampara Minera if it applies.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The jury values originality of style and of repertoire, musical and literary, and the singer's own artistic contributions, within the orthodoxy of each cante."},{"Title":"Cante - Grupo I: Tarantas","Source":"Bases del LXV Concurso de Cante Flamenco 2026, bases TERCERA to DUODECIMA","Sections":{"About":["Group I, mining cantes: Tarantas. A single prize.","The contestant sings one letra (verse) only."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Expenses paid to contestants at the selective tests: 30 euros for a local singer (home town less than 60 km from the test) and 150 euros for a non-local singer (more than 60 km).","Expenses paid to contestants who reach the semifinals: 30 euros for a local singer and 150 euros for a non-local singer.","A contestant in the final who wins no prize is paid 600 euros once, which replaces the semifinal expenses. Prize winners get no participation expenses.","The Lampara Minera winner must give at least four promotion recitals: one at the Gala de Premiados of the next festival and the others on dates the organisation decides.","The winners of the other Cante prizes, if they are not the Lampara Minera winner, must give at least one promotion recital on the date, at the place and on the terms the organisation decides.","For the promotion recitals the organisation pays only the travel and lodging of the winner and the accompanying guitarist. No fee is paid.","Documents to send by post: a photograph of the artist, an artistic curriculum, a recent video recording of the cantes you enter with, a bank certificate (or a copy of the savings book) showing you as holder or joint holder with an IBAN of a Spanish account, and a note saying whether you have your own guitarist or want one from the festival.","A contestant can perform at most four cantes, plus the cante of the draw for the Lampara Minera if it applies."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The jury values originality of style and of repertoire, musical and literary, and the singer's own artistic contributions, within the orthodoxy of each cante."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Group I, mining cantes: Tarantas. A single prize.\\n- The contestant sings one letra (verse) only.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Expenses paid to contestants at the selective tests: 30 euros for a local singer (home town less than 60 km from the test) and 150 euros for a non-local singer (more than 60 km).\\n- Expenses paid to contestants who reach the semifinals: 30 euros for a local singer and 150 euros for a non-local singer.\\n- A contestant in the final who wins no prize is paid 600 euros once, which replaces the semifinal expenses. Prize winners get no participation expenses.\\n- The Lampara Minera winner must give at least four promotion recitals: one at the Gala de Premiados of the next festival and the others on dates the organisation decides.\\n- The winners of the other Cante prizes, if they are not the Lampara Minera winner, must give at least one promotion recital on the date, at the place and on the terms the organisation decides.\\n- For the promotion recitals the organisation pays only the travel and lodging of the winner and the accompanying guitarist. No fee is paid.\\n- Documents to send by post: a photograph of the artist, an artistic curriculum, a recent video recording of the cantes you enter with, a bank certificate (or a copy of the savings book) showing you as holder or joint holder with an IBAN of a Spanish account, and a note saying whether you have your own guitarist or want one from the festival.\\n- A contestant can perform at most four cantes, plus the cante of the draw for the Lampara Minera if it applies.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The jury values originality of style and of repertoire, musical and literary, and the singer's own artistic contributions, within the orthodoxy of each cante."},{"Title":"Cante - Grupo I: Murcianas y otros cantes mineros","Source":"Bases del LXV Concurso de Cante Flamenco 2026, bases TERCERA to DUODECIMA","Sections":{"About":["Group I, mining cantes: Murcianas and other mining cantes (taranto, levantica, fandango minero, cantes de madrugada and others). A single prize.","The contestant sings one letra (verse) only."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Expenses paid to contestants at the selective tests: 30 euros for a local singer (home town less than 60 km from the test) and 150 euros for a non-local singer (more than 60 km).","Expenses paid to contestants who reach the semifinals: 30 euros for a local singer and 150 euros for a non-local singer.","A contestant in the final who wins no prize is paid 600 euros once, which replaces the semifinal expenses. Prize winners get no participation expenses.","The Lampara Minera winner must give at least four promotion recitals: one at the Gala de Premiados of the next festival and the others on dates the organisation decides.","The winners of the other Cante prizes, if they are not the Lampara Minera winner, must give at least one promotion recital on the date, at the place and on the terms the organisation decides.","For the promotion recitals the organisation pays only the travel and lodging of the winner and the accompanying guitarist. No fee is paid.","Documents to send by post: a photograph of the artist, an artistic curriculum, a recent video recording of the cantes you enter with, a bank certificate (or a copy of the savings book) showing you as holder or joint holder with an IBAN of a Spanish account, and a note saying whether you have your own guitarist or want one from the festival.","A contestant can perform at most four cantes, plus the cante of the draw for the Lampara Minera if it applies."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The jury values originality of style and of repertoire, musical and literary, and the singer's own artistic contributions, within the orthodoxy of each cante."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Group I, mining cantes: Murcianas and other mining cantes (taranto, levantica, fandango minero, cantes de madrugada and others). A single prize.\\n- The contestant sings one letra (verse) only.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Expenses paid to contestants at the selective tests: 30 euros for a local singer (home town less than 60 km from the test) and 150 euros for a non-local singer (more than 60 km).\\n- Expenses paid to contestants who reach the semifinals: 30 euros for a local singer and 150 euros for a non-local singer.\\n- A contestant in the final who wins no prize is paid 600 euros once, which replaces the semifinal expenses. Prize winners get no participation expenses.\\n- The Lampara Minera winner must give at least four promotion recitals: one at the Gala de Premiados of the next festival and the others on dates the organisation decides.\\n- The winners of the other Cante prizes, if they are not the Lampara Minera winner, must give at least one promotion recital on the date, at the place and on the terms the organisation decides.\\n- For the promotion recitals the organisation pays only the travel and lodging of the winner and the accompanying guitarist. No fee is paid.\\n- Documents to send by post: a photograph of the artist, an artistic curriculum, a recent video recording of the cantes you enter with, a bank certificate (or a copy of the savings book) showing you as holder or joint holder with an IBAN of a Spanish account, and a note saying whether you have your own guitarist or want one from the festival.\\n- A contestant can perform at most four cantes, plus the cante of the draw for the Lampara Minera if it applies.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The jury values originality of style and of repertoire, musical and literary, and the singer's own artistic contributions, within the orthodoxy of each cante."},{"Title":"Cante - Grupo II: Fandangos (Malaga, Granada, Cordoba, Huelva)","Source":"Bases del LXV Concurso de Cante Flamenco 2026, bases TERCERA to DUODECIMA","Sections":{"About":["Group II: cantes of Malaga, Granada, Cordoba and Huelva and other cantes derived from the Andalusian fandango. A single prize."],"TimeAndFormat":["The contestant sings one cante of this group, with two letras or a length of not more than 7 minutes."],"Rules":["Expenses paid to contestants at the selective tests: 30 euros for a local singer (home town less than 60 km from the test) and 150 euros for a non-local singer (more than 60 km).","Expenses paid to contestants who reach the semifinals: 30 euros for a local singer and 150 euros for a non-local singer.","A contestant in the final who wins no prize is paid 600 euros once, which replaces the semifinal expenses. Prize winners get no participation expenses.","The Lampara Minera winner must give at least four promotion recitals: one at the Gala de Premiados of the next festival and the others on dates the organisation decides.","The winners of the other Cante prizes, if they are not the Lampara Minera winner, must give at least one promotion recital on the date, at the place and on the terms the organisation decides.","For the promotion recitals the organisation pays only the travel and lodging of the winner and the accompanying guitarist. No fee is paid.","Documents to send by post: a photograph of the artist, an artistic curriculum, a recent video recording of the cantes you enter with, a bank certificate (or a copy of the savings book) showing you as holder or joint holder with an IBAN of a Spanish account, and a note saying whether you have your own guitarist or want one from the festival.","A contestant can perform at most four cantes, plus the cante of the draw for the Lampara Minera if it applies."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The jury values originality of style and of repertoire, musical and literary, and the singer's own artistic contributions, within the orthodoxy of each cante."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Group II: cantes of Malaga, Granada, Cordoba and Huelva and other cantes derived from the Andalusian fandango. A single prize.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The contestant sings one cante of this group, with two letras or a length of not more than 7 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Expenses paid to contestants at the selective tests: 30 euros for a local singer (home town less than 60 km from the test) and 150 euros for a non-local singer (more than 60 km).\\n- Expenses paid to contestants who reach the semifinals: 30 euros for a local singer and 150 euros for a non-local singer.\\n- A contestant in the final who wins no prize is paid 600 euros once, which replaces the semifinal expenses. Prize winners get no participation expenses.\\n- The Lampara Minera winner must give at least four promotion recitals: one at the Gala de Premiados of the next festival and the others on dates the organisation decides.\\n- The winners of the other Cante prizes, if they are not the Lampara Minera winner, must give at least one promotion recital on the date, at the place and on the terms the organisation decides.\\n- For the promotion recitals the organisation pays only the travel and lodging of the winner and the accompanying guitarist. No fee is paid.\\n- Documents to send by post: a photograph of the artist, an artistic curriculum, a recent video recording of the cantes you enter with, a bank certificate (or a copy of the savings book) showing you as holder or joint holder with an IBAN of a Spanish account, and a note saying whether you have your own guitarist or want one from the festival.\\n- A contestant can perform at most four cantes, plus the cante of the draw for the Lampara Minera if it applies.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The jury values originality of style and of repertoire, musical and literary, and the singer's own artistic contributions, within the orthodoxy of each cante."},{"Title":"Cante - Grupo III A: Tonas, Siguiriyas, Soleares, Bulerias por Solea, Canas, Polos, Livianas, Serranas","Source":"Bases del LXV Concurso de Cante Flamenco 2026, bases TERCERA to DUODECIMA","Sections":{"About":["Group III A (cantes of Lower Andalusia): tonas, siguiriyas, soleares, bulerias por solea, canas, polos, livianas and serranas. A single prize."],"TimeAndFormat":["The chosen cante lasts at most 7 minutes."],"Rules":["Expenses paid to contestants at the selective tests: 30 euros for a local singer (home town less than 60 km from the test) and 150 euros for a non-local singer (more than 60 km).","Expenses paid to contestants who reach the semifinals: 30 euros for a local singer and 150 euros for a non-local singer.","A contestant in the final who wins no prize is paid 600 euros once, which replaces the semifinal expenses. Prize winners get no participation expenses.","The Lampara Minera winner must give at least four promotion recitals: one at the Gala de Premiados of the next festival and the others on dates the organisation decides.","The winners of the other Cante prizes, if they are not the Lampara Minera winner, must give at least one promotion recital on the date, at the place and on the terms the organisation decides.","For the promotion recitals the organisation pays only the travel and lodging of the winner and the accompanying guitarist. No fee is paid.","Documents to send by post: a photograph of the artist, an artistic curriculum, a recent video recording of the cantes you enter with, a bank certificate (or a copy of the savings book) showing you as holder or joint holder with an IBAN of a Spanish account, and a note saying whether you have your own guitarist or want one from the festival.","A contestant can perform at most four cantes, plus the cante of the draw for the Lampara Minera if it applies."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The jury values originality of style and of repertoire, musical and literary, and the singer's own artistic contributions, within the orthodoxy of each cante."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Group III A (cantes of Lower Andalusia): tonas, siguiriyas, soleares, bulerias por solea, canas, polos, livianas and serranas. A single prize.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The chosen cante lasts at most 7 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Expenses paid to contestants at the selective tests: 30 euros for a local singer (home town less than 60 km from the test) and 150 euros for a non-local singer (more than 60 km).\\n- Expenses paid to contestants who reach the semifinals: 30 euros for a local singer and 150 euros for a non-local singer.\\n- A contestant in the final who wins no prize is paid 600 euros once, which replaces the semifinal expenses. Prize winners get no participation expenses.\\n- The Lampara Minera winner must give at least four promotion recitals: one at the Gala de Premiados of the next festival and the others on dates the organisation decides.\\n- The winners of the other Cante prizes, if they are not the Lampara Minera winner, must give at least one promotion recital on the date, at the place and on the terms the organisation decides.\\n- For the promotion recitals the organisation pays only the travel and lodging of the winner and the accompanying guitarist. No fee is paid.\\n- Documents to send by post: a photograph of the artist, an artistic curriculum, a recent video recording of the cantes you enter with, a bank certificate (or a copy of the savings book) showing you as holder or joint holder with an IBAN of a Spanish account, and a note saying whether you have your own guitarist or want one from the festival.\\n- A contestant can perform at most four cantes, plus the cante of the draw for the Lampara Minera if it applies.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The jury values originality of style and of repertoire, musical and literary, and the singer's own artistic contributions, within the orthodoxy of each cante."},{"Title":"Cante - Grupo III B: Bulerias, Cantinas, Tangos, Tientos, Peteneras, Farrucas, Fandangos personales","Source":"Bases del LXV Concurso de Cante Flamenco 2026, bases TERCERA to DUODECIMA","Sections":{"About":["Group III B (cantes of Lower Andalusia): bulerias, cantinas, tangos, tientos, peteneras, farrucas, personal fandangos, and other kinds of cante that the contestants propose and the jury accepts in this section at the selective tests. A single prize."],"TimeAndFormat":["The chosen cante lasts at most 5 minutes."],"Rules":["Expenses paid to contestants at the selective tests: 30 euros for a local singer (home town less than 60 km from the test) and 150 euros for a non-local singer (more than 60 km).","Expenses paid to contestants who reach the semifinals: 30 euros for a local singer and 150 euros for a non-local singer.","A contestant in the final who wins no prize is paid 600 euros once, which replaces the semifinal expenses. Prize winners get no participation expenses.","The Lampara Minera winner must give at least four promotion recitals: one at the Gala de Premiados of the next festival and the others on dates the organisation decides.","The winners of the other Cante prizes, if they are not the Lampara Minera winner, must give at least one promotion recital on the date, at the place and on the terms the organisation decides.","For the promotion recitals the organisation pays only the travel and lodging of the winner and the accompanying guitarist. No fee is paid.","Documents to send by post: a photograph of the artist, an artistic curriculum, a recent video recording of the cantes you enter with, a bank certificate (or a copy of the savings book) showing you as holder or joint holder with an IBAN of a Spanish account, and a note saying whether you have your own guitarist or want one from the festival.","A contestant can perform at most four cantes, plus the cante of the draw for the Lampara Minera if it applies."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The jury values originality of style and of repertoire, musical and literary, and the singer's own artistic contributions, within the orthodoxy of each cante."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Group III B (cantes of Lower Andalusia): bulerias, cantinas, tangos, tientos, peteneras, farrucas, personal fandangos, and other kinds of cante that the contestants propose and the jury accepts in this section at the selective tests. A single prize.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The chosen cante lasts at most 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Expenses paid to contestants at the selective tests: 30 euros for a local singer (home town less than 60 km from the test) and 150 euros for a non-local singer (more than 60 km).\\n- Expenses paid to contestants who reach the semifinals: 30 euros for a local singer and 150 euros for a non-local singer.\\n- A contestant in the final who wins no prize is paid 600 euros once, which replaces the semifinal expenses. Prize winners get no participation expenses.\\n- The Lampara Minera winner must give at least four promotion recitals: one at the Gala de Premiados of the next festival and the others on dates the organisation decides.\\n- The winners of the other Cante prizes, if they are not the Lampara Minera winner, must give at least one promotion recital on the date, at the place and on the terms the organisation decides.\\n- For the promotion recitals the organisation pays only the travel and lodging of the winner and the accompanying guitarist. No fee is paid.\\n- Documents to send by post: a photograph of the artist, an artistic curriculum, a recent video recording of the cantes you enter with, a bank certificate (or a copy of the savings book) showing you as holder or joint holder with an IBAN of a Spanish account, and a note saying whether you have your own guitarist or want one from the festival.\\n- A contestant can perform at most four cantes, plus the cante of the draw for the Lampara Minera if it applies.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The jury values originality of style and of repertoire, musical and literary, and the singer's own artistic contributions, within the orthodoxy of each cante."},{"Title":"Cante - Cantaores Jovenes","Source":"Bases del LXV Concurso de Cante Flamenco 2026, bases TERCERA to DUODECIMA","Sections":{"About":["Special prize for young singers (Cantaores Jovenes). It is given only to a contestant who won none of the other prizes of the Cante contest in this edition or in earlier editions."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Expenses paid to contestants at the selective tests: 30 euros for a local singer (home town less than 60 km from the test) and 150 euros for a non-local singer (more than 60 km).","Expenses paid to contestants who reach the semifinals: 30 euros for a local singer and 150 euros for a non-local singer.","A contestant in the final who wins no prize is paid 600 euros once, which replaces the semifinal expenses. Prize winners get no participation expenses.","The Lampara Minera winner must give at least four promotion recitals: one at the Gala de Premiados of the next festival and the others on dates the organisation decides.","The winners of the other Cante prizes, if they are not the Lampara Minera winner, must give at least one promotion recital on the date, at the place and on the terms the organisation decides.","For the promotion recitals the organisation pays only the travel and lodging of the winner and the accompanying guitarist. No fee is paid.","Documents to send by post: a photograph of the artist, an artistic curriculum, a recent video recording of the cantes you enter with, a bank certificate (or a copy of the savings book) showing you as holder or joint holder with an IBAN of a Spanish account, and a note saying whether you have your own guitarist or want one from the festival.","A contestant can perform at most four cantes, plus the cante of the draw for the Lampara Minera if it applies."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The jury values originality of style and of repertoire, musical and literary, and the singer's own artistic contributions, within the orthodoxy of each cante."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Special prize for young singers (Cantaores Jovenes). It is given only to a contestant who won none of the other prizes of the Cante contest in this edition or in earlier editions.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Expenses paid to contestants at the selective tests: 30 euros for a local singer (home town less than 60 km from the test) and 150 euros for a non-local singer (more than 60 km).\\n- Expenses paid to contestants who reach the semifinals: 30 euros for a local singer and 150 euros for a non-local singer.\\n- A contestant in the final who wins no prize is paid 600 euros once, which replaces the semifinal expenses. Prize winners get no participation expenses.\\n- The Lampara Minera winner must give at least four promotion recitals: one at the Gala de Premiados of the next festival and the others on dates the organisation decides.\\n- The winners of the other Cante prizes, if they are not the Lampara Minera winner, must give at least one promotion recital on the date, at the place and on the terms the organisation decides.\\n- For the promotion recitals the organisation pays only the travel and lodging of the winner and the accompanying guitarist. No fee is paid.\\n- Documents to send by post: a photograph of the artist, an artistic curriculum, a recent video recording of the cantes you enter with, a bank certificate (or a copy of the savings book) showing you as holder or joint holder with an IBAN of a Spanish account, and a note saying whether you have your own guitarist or want one from the festival.\\n- A contestant can perform at most four cantes, plus the cante of the draw for the Lampara Minera if it applies.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The jury values originality of style and of repertoire, musical and literary, and the singer's own artistic contributions, within the orthodoxy of each cante."},{"Title":"Guitarra Flamenca","Source":"Bases del XLVI Concurso de Guitarra Flamenca 2026, bases TERCERA to UNDECIMA","Sections":{"About":["The contestant plays two toques (guitar pieces)."],"TimeAndFormat":["The whole performance in a selective test, the semifinal or the final lasts at most 15 minutes. The contestant decides how to divide the time between the two toques.","The organisation asks, the day before each performance, which works the guitarist will play."],"Rules":["One toque minero (mining toque) is obligatory.","The other toque is any flamenco toque the contestant chooses, but it must be a rhythmic toque with a clear beat (compas).","In the final the rhythmic toque must be different from the rhythmic toque played in the semifinal.","During the semifinals and the final the guitarist can be accompanied by at most two palmeros and one percussionist. This must be on the registration form and the contestant pays the accompanists.","Documents to send by post: a photograph of the artist, an artistic curriculum, a digital video recording of the toques, and a bank certificate (or a copy of the savings book) showing you as holder or joint holder with an IBAN of a Spanish account. A video of the toques must also be attached to online registration.","Expenses paid to contestants at the selective tests: 30 euros for a local guitarist (home town less than 60 km from the test) and 150 euros for a non-local guitarist (more than 60 km).","Expenses paid to contestants who reach the semifinals: 30 euros for a local guitarist and 150 euros for a non-local guitarist.","A finalist who wins no prize is paid 600 euros once, which replaces the semifinal expenses. Prize winners get no participation expenses.","The first prize winner must give at least three promotion recitals: one at the Gala de Premiados of the next festival and the others on dates the organisation decides.","For the promotion recitals the organisation pays only the travel and lodging of the winner. No fee is paid.","The jury can declare any prize void, and can choose nobody for the final."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["The capo (cejilla) is never allowed."],"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":["The selective tests are held between June and July according to base SEPTIMA. Annex I of the same bases says May to June."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The contestant plays two toques (guitar pieces).\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The whole performance in a selective test, the semifinal or the final lasts at most 15 minutes. The contestant decides how to divide the time between the two toques.\\n- The organisation asks, the day before each performance, which works the guitarist will play.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- One toque minero (mining toque) is obligatory.\\n- The other toque is any flamenco toque the contestant chooses, but it must be a rhythmic toque with a clear beat (compas).\\n- In the final the rhythmic toque must be different from the rhythmic toque played in the semifinal.\\n- During the semifinals and the final the guitarist can be accompanied by at most two palmeros and one percussionist. This must be on the registration form and the contestant pays the accompanists.\\n- Documents to send by post: a photograph of the artist, an artistic curriculum, a digital video recording of the toques, and a bank certificate (or a copy of the savings book) showing you as holder or joint holder with an IBAN of a Spanish account. A video of the toques must also be attached to online registration.\\n- Expenses paid to contestants at the selective tests: 30 euros for a local guitarist (home town less than 60 km from the test) and 150 euros for a non-local guitarist (more than 60 km).\\n- Expenses paid to contestants who reach the semifinals: 30 euros for a local guitarist and 150 euros for a non-local guitarist.\\n- A finalist who wins no prize is paid 600 euros once, which replaces the semifinal expenses. Prize winners get no participation expenses.\\n- The first prize winner must give at least three promotion recitals: one at the Gala de Premiados of the next festival and the others on dates the organisation decides.\\n- For the promotion recitals the organisation pays only the travel and lodging of the winner. No fee is paid.\\n- The jury can declare any prize void, and can choose nobody for the final.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- The capo (cejilla) is never allowed.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- The selective tests are held between June and July according to base SEPTIMA. Annex I of the same bases says May to June."},{"Title":"Baile Flamenco","Source":"Bases del XXXII Concurso de Baile Flamenco 2026, bases TERCERA to UNDECIMA and Annex I","Sections":{"About":["The contestant dances two flamenco dances. The jury values both dances together and gives the prize for the best and most complete interpretation."],"TimeAndFormat":["In a semifinal, the whole performance lasts at most 20 minutes. The contestant decides how to divide the time between the two dances.","The organisation asks, the day before each performance, which works the dancer will perform."],"Rules":["Semifinals: one dance por taranto is obligatory. The other dance is any flamenco dance the contestant chooses.","Final: one dance por taranto is obligatory. The other dance is any flamenco dance the contestant chooses, and it must be different from the one performed in the semifinal.","Documents to send by post: a photograph of the artist, an artistic curriculum, a bank certificate (or a copy of the savings book) showing you as holder or joint holder with an IBAN of a Spanish account, the technical needs for the performance, a list of the group members (name, surname and role), and a video of the performance (.mp4, .mov or similar).","Expenses paid at the selective tests (for the dancer and the whole group): 90 euros for a local dancer (home town less than 60 km from the test) and 300 euros for a non-local dancer (more than 60 km).","Expenses paid to contestants who reach the semifinals: 1,000 euros.","A finalist who wins no prize is paid 1,000 euros once, which replaces the semifinal expenses. Prize winners get no participation expenses.","The winner of the Baile prize must give at least two promotion recitals: one at the Gala de Premiados of the next festival and the other on a date the organisation decides.","For the promotion recitals the organisation pays only the travel and lodging of the winner and up to 3 accompanying artists. No fee is paid.","The jury can choose nobody for the final, and then the prize is void."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":["The festival web page says the dance contest now has two forms of artistic expression, and that contestants can win the Desplante prize in a men's and a women's category. The bases do not describe these forms or categories.","The bases print no time limit for the final."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The contestant dances two flamenco dances. The jury values both dances together and gives the prize for the best and most complete interpretation.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- In a semifinal, the whole performance lasts at most 20 minutes. The contestant decides how to divide the time between the two dances.\\n- The organisation asks, the day before each performance, which works the dancer will perform.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Semifinals: one dance por taranto is obligatory. The other dance is any flamenco dance the contestant chooses.\\n- Final: one dance por taranto is obligatory. The other dance is any flamenco dance the contestant chooses, and it must be different from the one performed in the semifinal.\\n- Documents to send by post: a photograph of the artist, an artistic curriculum, a bank certificate (or a copy of the savings book) showing you as holder or joint holder with an IBAN of a Spanish account, the technical needs for the performance, a list of the group members (name, surname and role), and a video of the performance (.mp4, .mov or similar).\\n- Expenses paid at the selective tests (for the dancer and the whole group): 90 euros for a local dancer (home town less than 60 km from the test) and 300 euros for a non-local dancer (more than 60 km).\\n- Expenses paid to contestants who reach the semifinals: 1,000 euros.\\n- A finalist who wins no prize is paid 1,000 euros once, which replaces the semifinal expenses. Prize winners get no participation expenses.\\n- The winner of the Baile prize must give at least two promotion recitals: one at the Gala de Premiados of the next festival and the other on a date the organisation decides.\\n- For the promotion recitals the organisation pays only the travel and lodging of the winner and up to 3 accompanying artists. No fee is paid.\\n- The jury can choose nobody for the final, and then the prize is void.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- The festival web page says the dance contest now has two forms of artistic expression, and that contestants can win the Desplante prize in a men's and a women's category. The bases do not describe these forms or categories.\\n- The bases print no time limit for the final."},{"Title":"Instrumentista Flamenco","Source":"Bases del XVIII Concurso de Instrumentista Flamenco 2026, bases SEGUNDA to UNDECIMA and Annex I","Sections":{"About":["Every kind of instrument is accepted except the flamenco guitar, which has its own contest. A contestant can enter alone or as part of a group."],"TimeAndFormat":["The performance in the semifinals or the final lasts at most 15 minutes. The contestant decides how to divide the time between the two works.","The organisation asks, the day before each performance, which works the contestant will play.","On {{InstrumentistaFinalWorksTime}}, all finalists must say which works they will play in the final."],"Rules":["The contestant plays one or two works, as the contestant decides. The works must be written in the registration form.","The works must be of a recognisable flamenco character. They can be new pieces or arrangements of existing pieces.","The works must clearly bring to mind mining airs (mineras, cartageneras, tarantas, tarantos, rondenas and others): either one of the two pieces is about these styles, or part or all of a single work is.","The works must also have a rhythmic part, either in one of the two works or in part of a single work.","In the final, one work with a mining air or style is obligatory.","The selected artists must agree their technical needs with the organisation. The organisation can refuse some demands, and a refusal can be a reason for disqualification.","Documents to send by post: a photograph of the artist, an artistic curriculum, a bank certificate (or a copy of the savings book) showing you as holder or joint holder with an IBAN of a Spanish account, a digital audiovisual demo (DVD, CD, USB or a video file transfer such as .mp4 or .mov) of the works you enter with, the technical needs, and a list of the group members (name, surname and role).","The jury chooses the semifinalists by watching the video material. There are no selective tests.","Expenses paid to contestants who reach the semifinals (for the instrumentalist and the whole group, for lodging and meals for the contest day): 90 euros for a local contestant (home town less than 60 km from the test) and 300 euros for a non-local contestant (more than 60 km).","A finalist who wins no prize is paid 1,000 euros once, which replaces the semifinal expenses. Prize winners get no participation expenses.","The first prize winner must give at least three promotion recitals: one at the Gala de Premiados of the next festival and the others on dates the organisation decides.","For the promotion recitals the organisation pays only the travel and lodging of the winner and up to 3 accompanying artists. No fee is paid.","The jury can choose nobody for the final, and then the prize is void."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Every kind of instrument is accepted except the flamenco guitar, which has its own contest. A contestant can enter alone or as part of a group.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The performance in the semifinals or the final lasts at most 15 minutes. The contestant decides how to divide the time between the two works.\\n- The organisation asks, the day before each performance, which works the contestant will play.\\n- On {{InstrumentistaFinalWorksTime}}, all finalists must say which works they will play in the final.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The contestant plays one or two works, as the contestant decides. The works must be written in the registration form.\\n- The works must be of a recognisable flamenco character. They can be new pieces or arrangements of existing pieces.\\n- The works must clearly bring to mind mining airs (mineras, cartageneras, tarantas, tarantos, rondenas and others): either one of the two pieces is about these styles, or part or all of a single work is.\\n- The works must also have a rhythmic part, either in one of the two works or in part of a single work.\\n- In the final, one work with a mining air or style is obligatory.\\n- The selected artists must agree their technical needs with the organisation. The organisation can refuse some demands, and a refusal can be a reason for disqualification.\\n- Documents to send by post: a photograph of the artist, an artistic curriculum, a bank certificate (or a copy of the savings book) showing you as holder or joint holder with an IBAN of a Spanish account, a digital audiovisual demo (DVD, CD, USB or a video file transfer such as .mp4 or .mov) of the works you enter with, the technical needs, and a list of the group members (name, surname and role).\\n- The jury chooses the semifinalists by watching the video material. There are no selective tests.\\n- Expenses paid to contestants who reach the semifinals (for the instrumentalist and the whole group, for lodging and meals for the contest day): 90 euros for a local contestant (home town less than 60 km from the test) and 300 euros for a non-local contestant (more than 60 km).\\n- A finalist who wins no prize is paid 1,000 euros once, which replaces the semifinal expenses. Prize winners get no participation expenses.\\n- The first prize winner must give at least three promotion recitals: one at the Gala de Premiados of the next festival and the others on dates the organisation decides.\\n- For the promotion recitals the organisation pays only the travel and lodging of the winner and up to 3 accompanying artists. No fee is paid.\\n- The jury can choose nobody for the final, and then the prize is void."}]`),i=[],r=[{Key:"FestivalDates",Kind:"date",Label:"Festival dates",Value:"29 July to 8 August 2026",Source:"Festival web page Bases de los concursos 2026, registration notice"},{Key:"ContestDates",Kind:"date",Label:"Contest dates",Value:"5, 6, 7 and 8 August 2026",Source:"Festival web page Bases de los concursos 2026; Bases del LXV Concurso de Cante Flamenco 2026, base PRIMERA"},{Key:"SemifinalDates",Kind:"date",Label:"Semifinal dates",Value:"5, 6 and 7 August 2026",Source:"Bases del LXV Concurso de Cante Flamenco 2026, Annex I, Tercera"},{Key:"FinalDate",Kind:"date",Label:"Final date",Value:"2026-08-08",Source:"Bases del LXV Concurso de Cante Flamenco 2026, Annex I, Cuarta"},{Key:"RegistrationDeadline",Kind:"date",Label:"Last date to register for Cante, Guitarra and Baile (extended)",Value:"2026-06-20",Source:"Festival web page Bases de los concursos 2026, registration notice (the bases print 1 June 2026)"},{Key:"InstrumentistaDeadline",Kind:"date",Label:"Last date to register for Instrumentista",Value:"2026-07-01",Source:"Festival web page Bases de los concursos 2026; Bases del XVIII Concurso de Instrumentista Flamenco 2026, base OCTAVA"},{Key:"SelectiveTestsPeriod",Kind:"text",Label:"Selective tests period",Value:"in June and July 2026. The organisation gives the places and dates in advance.",Source:"Bases del LXV Concurso de Cante Flamenco 2026, base NOVENA"},{Key:"SemifinalResultsTime",Kind:"time",Label:"When the semifinal results are published",Value:"in the early hours of 7 to 8 August 2026",Source:"Bases del LXV Concurso de Cante Flamenco 2026, Annex I, Tercera b"},{Key:"LamparaDrawTime",Kind:"time",Label:"Public draw for the Lampara Minera",Value:"Saturday 8 August 2026 at 11:00",Source:"Bases del LXV Concurso de Cante Flamenco 2026, base TERCERA, conditions"},{Key:"InstrumentistaFinalWorksTime",Kind:"time",Label:"Finalists state their Instrumentista works",Value:"Saturday 8 August 2026 at 11:00",Source:"Bases del XVIII Concurso de Instrumentista Flamenco 2026, base QUINTA"},{Key:"FestivalVenue",Kind:"address",Label:"Festival and contest venue",Value:{Name:"Festival Internacional del Cante de las Minas",Address:"",City:"La Union, Murcia",MapUrl:"",Directions:""},Source:"Bases del LXV Concurso de Cante Flamenco 2026, base PRIMERA; web page"},{Key:"LamparaDrawVenue",Kind:"address",Label:"Lampara Minera draw venue",Value:{Name:"Salon de Actos, Casa del Pinon",Address:"",City:"La Union",MapUrl:"",Directions:""},Source:"Bases del LXV Concurso de Cante Flamenco 2026, base TERCERA, conditions"},{Key:"RegistrationAddress",Kind:"address",Label:"Postal registration address",Value:{Name:"Fundacion Cante de las Minas",Address:"Calle Mayor 55, Edificio Casa del Pinon, 2a Planta, 30360",City:"La Union (Murcia)",MapUrl:"",Directions:""},Source:"Bases del LXV Concurso de Cante Flamenco 2026, base SEPTIMA"},{Key:"ContestsContact",Kind:"contact",Label:"Contests email for audiovisual demos",Value:{Name:"Fundacion Cante de las Minas, contests",Role:"Send demo videos or audio links",Phone:"",WhatsApp:"",Email:"concursos@festivalcantedelasminas.org"},Source:"Festival web page Bases de los concursos 2026, online registration form"},{Key:"FestivalWebsite",Kind:"link",Label:"Festival website",Value:"www.festivalcantedelasminas.org",Source:"Bases del LXV Concurso de Cante Flamenco 2026, base SEPTIMA"},{Key:"TourCities",Kind:"text",Label:"Cities planned for Las Minas Flamenco Tour 26/27",Value:"Badajoz, Zaragoza, Segovia, Valladolid, Lugo, Malaga, Boadilla, Madrid, Barcelona, Murcia, Cartagena, Molina de Segura, Alicante, Granada, Jerez, Sevilla, Cadiz, Cordoba, Jaen, Huelva, Valencia, Tarragona, Gijon, Oviedo, Santander, Bilbao and San Sebastian.",Source:"Bases del LXV Concurso de Cante Flamenco 2026, Annex II"},{Key:"Announcements",Kind:"news",Label:"News printed on the bases page",Value:[{Date:"",Title:"Registration period extended",Text:"The registration period for the Cante, Guitarra, Baile and Instrumentista contests of the 65th Festival Internacional del Cante de las Minas is extended. Registration ends on 20 June, except Instrumentista, which stays open until 1 July. The contests are held on 5, 6, 7 and 8 August 2026.",Url:"https://festivalcantedelasminas.org/bases-concursos-2026/"}],Source:"Festival web page Bases de los concursos 2026, header notice"}],h=[{Claim:"All rules, eligibility, prizes, phases and dates on the registration page are read from the organiser's own 2026 bases and registration page.",SourceType:"Primary - the event's own rules document",Source:"Bases de los concursos 2026 (LXV edicion)",Url:"https://festivalcantedelasminas.org/bases-concursos-2026/"}],c={TemplateKey:e,Year:2026,Note:t,Page:a,ParticipantTypes:n,AgeGroups:o,Competitions:s,CompetitionAgeGroups:i,Variables:r,Evidence:h};export{o as AgeGroups,i as CompetitionAgeGroups,s as Competitions,h as Evidence,t as Note,a as Page,n as ParticipantTypes,e as TemplateKey,r as Variables,l as Year,c as default};
